Link only the applets under test.

The kernel's ext4 writer caches at most 128 inodes per mount and never evicts
one, so runtest's link for every implemented applet exhausted it before any
test ran. With applet arguments only those applets get links; without
arguments every applet is still linked.

--- a/testsuite/runtest
+++ b/testsuite/runtest
@@ -124,7 +124,7 @@
 rm -rf "$LINKSDIR" 2>/dev/null
 
 mkdir "$LINKSDIR" 2>/dev/null
-for i in $implemented; do
+for i in $applets; do
 	# Note: if $LINKSDIR/applet exists, we do not overwrite it.
 	# Useful if one wants to run tests against a standard utility,
 	# not an applet.
